..\ndrwxr-xr-x@ 4 alexander  wheel  128 Nov 16 22:36 moneyfmt-2.0.0\n\nvendor-updates/moneyfmt-2.0.0:\ntotal 8\ndrwxr-xr-x@ 4 alexander  wheel  128 Nov 16 22:36 .\ndrwxr-xr-x@ 3 alexander  wheel   96 Nov 16 22:36 ..\n-rw-r--r--@ 1 alexander  wheel  491 Oct 28 23:27 CHANGELOG.md\ndrwxr-xr-x@ 3 alexander  wheel   96 Nov 16 22:36 moneyfmt\n\nvendor-updates/moneyfmt-2.0.0/moneyfmt:\ntotal 8\ndrwxr-xr-x@ 3 alexander  wheel    96 Nov 16 22:36 .\ndrwxr-xr-x@ 4 alexander  wheel   128 Nov 16 22:36 ..\n-rw-r--r--@ 1 alexander  wheel  1630 Oct 28 23:27 __init__.py\n---GIT LOG---\n13f9f71 fixture\n---STATUS---\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"ls -laR vendor vendor-updates; echo \"---GIT LOG---\"; git log --oneline -20; echo \"---STATUS---\"; git status --short","time":{"start":1794861447746,"end":1794861448110}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"Let me check git log and status, and the vendor-updates dir structure more carefully (any other files like dist-info, RECORD, etc.).\n\nThe task says \"the vendored copy in `vendor/moneyfmt/` becomes 2.0.0 (the released files, unmodified)\". So the released files from `vendor-updates/moneyfmt-2.0.0/` should be copied to `vendor/moneyfmt/`. Let's check if there's more than `__init__.py` in the moneyfmt package of the update dir.\n\nAlso, note that `vendor-updates/moneyfmt-2.0.0/` contains `CHANGELOG.md` at the top level and `moneyfmt/__init__.py`. The released files for the package would be `moneyfmt/__init__.py`. Does the vendor dir include a CHANGELOG? Currently vendor/ only has moneyfmt/__init__.py. So the released package files = moneyfmt/__init__.py. Hmm, but \"the released files, unmodified\" — maybe there are hidden files. Let me check with ls -la.\n\nAlso let me check git history for hints.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_1e6143a0700173eGIJisLl8i8W","sessionID":"ses_e19ec4786ffeqnGAoXEPfPmRLE","messageID":"msg_1e614315d001MfrXS643yl4XRf"}}
