{"type":"text","timestamp":1794861987320,"sessionID":"ses_e19ec4786ffeqnGAoXEPfPmRLE","part":{"id":"prt_1e61c24ca001EnBN05BEOtkHvP","messageID":"msg_1e61c1c8d001bxxNaq2ZM7T89A","sessionID":"ses_e19ec4786ffeqnGAoXEPfPmRLE","type":"text","text":"Done. Changes:\n\n- `vendor/moneyfmt/__init__.py` — replaced with the 2.0.0 release file, byte-identical to `vendor-updates/moneyfmt-2.0.0/moneyfmt/__init__.py` (`cmp` verified); `requirements.txt` now pins `moneyfmt==2.0.0`.\n- `invoicer/totals.py:8` — `MoneyError` → `MoneyFormatError`; `Line.amount` is now `Decimal` (coerced in `__post_init__` so directly-built lines stay usable); `total()` sums with a `Decimal(\"0\")` seed so an empty invoice still formats; `format_money(..., currency=CURRENCY)` uses the new keyword-only currency.\n- `tests/test_moneyfmt_api.py` (new) — asserts the vendored lib is 2.0.0, the error class rename, `format_money`'s Decimal-only/keyword-only contract, exact decimal totals (`0.1 + 0.2` == `Decimal(\"0.30\")`, not the float artifact), and CLI stdout/stderr/exit codes. It fails against 1.4.0 and against a half-adapted upgrade that keeps floats; the pre-existing tests pass in both cases.\n\nVerification: `python -m unittest discover -s tests` → 13 tests OK. A 22-case CLI battery (stdout, stderr, exit status) is identical before/after except three cases caused by 2.0.0's *added* behaviour, not by the adaptation:\n\n- `A=CHF 49.99`: 2.0.0 added the `CHF` symbol, so it is now parsed as `€49.99` instead of erroring.\n- `A=NaN` / `A=Infinity`: 2.0.0 rejects them; the old code crashed with an uncaught `decimal.InvalidOperation` traceback (exit 1), now it is a clean `error: cannot read amount 'NaN'` (exit 2).\n\nTell me if you want the CHF case kept erroring (the invoicer is EUR-only, so I can reject foreign symbols explicitly) — I left the code free of special-casing since it is inherent to the library upgrade.","time":{"start":1794861966538,"end":1794861987291}}}
